  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q28-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "28",
    "prompt": "A page of a book is to have $80\\text{ cm}^2$ of printed material.\nThere is to be a $2\\text{ cm}$ margin at the top and bottom and a $1\\text{ cm}$ margin on each side.\nLet the page have width $x$ and height $y$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q28-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $(y-4)(x-2)=80$ and hence that $y=4+\\dfrac{80}{x-2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(y-4)(x-2)=80$, hence $y=4+\\dfrac{80}{x-2}$.",
          "worked": "The area of printed material is $80\\text{ cm}^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(y-2-2)(x-1-1)&=80\\\\(y-4)(x-2)&=80\\\\xy-2y-4x+8&=80\\\\y(x-2)&=4(x-2)+80\\\\y&=4+\\frac{80}{x-2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q28-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that the area of the page is $A=\\dfrac{4x^2+72x}{x-2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=\\dfrac{4x^2+72x}{x-2}$.",
          "worked": "Substitute $y=4+\\dfrac{80}{x-2}$ into $A=xy$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=x\\left(4+\\frac{80}{x-2}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac{x(4x-8+80)}{x-2}\\\\A&=\\frac{x(4x+72)}{x-2}\\\\A&=\\frac{4x^2+72x}{x-2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q28-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use the quotient rule to show that $\\dfrac{dA}{dx}=\\dfrac{4(x^2-4x-36)}{(x-2)^2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{dA}{dx}=\\dfrac{4(x^2-4x-36)}{(x-2)^2}$.",
          "worked": "With $u=4x^2+72x$ and $v=x-2$, the quotient rule gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dA}{dx}&=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}\\\\\\frac{dA}{dx}&=\\frac{(x-2)(8x+72)-(4x^2+72x)}{(x-2)^2}\\\\\\frac{dA}{dx}&=\\frac{4x^2-16x-144}{(x-2)^2}\\\\\\frac{dA}{dx}&=\\frac{4(x^2-4x-36)}{(x-2)^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q28-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What should be the dimensions of the page in order to use the least amount of paper?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Width $2(\\sqrt{10}+1)\\text{ cm}$ and height $4(\\sqrt{10}+1)\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": {
